{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And if his offering is from the flock</b> — This section (verses 10–13) deals with the burnt offering of the flock, and its law is like the law of the burnt offering of cattle in every respect. Therefore it is abbreviated here and does not mention \"and he shall lean his hand and it shall be accepted.\" And He added, saying, \"on the side of the altar northward, before YHWH\" (Leviticus 1:11), to explain that \"before YHWH\" written concerning the cattle (Leviticus 1:5) is the side of the altar on the north. And the meaning of \"side of the altar\" — its side, and it is on the north, teaching that the ramp of the altar is on the south, and there are the faces of the altar of which it is said concerning them, \"before YHWH, in front of the face of the altar\" (Leviticus 6:7). And the reason that the slaughter is on the north I have already explained. And it says simply \"on the altar all around\" because it is the altar already mentioned (Leviticus 1:5), which is at the entrance of the Tent of Meeting. And it does not mention \"and he shall flay,\" for it has already been mentioned (Leviticus 1:6). And it says, \"and the priest shall arrange them,\" to teach that one priest suffices, as I have explained (Ramban on Leviticus 1:6), for the sections teach one from the other: what is lacking in one will be explained in another."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:49:24.255925058Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}